<header class="guide-hero wrap"><p class="eyebrow">Getting started</p><h1>Your site. Your form.<br>A clear path to the inbox.</h1><p class="lead">Start with the experimental local Codex client. Review each change, publish explicitly and verify a synthetic receipt.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/register">Create an account</a><a class="button secondary" href="/login">Sign in</a></div></header>
<div class="wrap guide-layout"><nav class="guide-nav" aria-label="Getting started steps"><strong>On this page</strong><a href="#prerequisites">Before you start</a><a href="#connection">1. Account and connection</a><a href="#draft">2. Create a draft</a><a href="#integration">3. Connect your site</a><a href="#publish">4. Review and publish</a><a href="#receipt">5. Verify receipt</a></nav><div class="guide-body">
<section id="prerequisites"><h2>Before you start</h2><p>You need a site you can edit, an account with access to the intended workspace, Python 3 and the local Codex client from the GoFormX source. The client uses Python's standard library.</p><div class="callout"><p><strong>Local workflow verified. Hosted setup is still manual.</strong> The September 29 two-site rehearsal used disposable local GoFormX services. The live personal-site form was verified separately. There is no one-click Codex connector or verified setup path for other assistants.</p></div><p>Use the <a href="https://github.com/goformx/goformx/blob/b5308f5c2a6df7d86506a4adca21f5b2bfab4e1d/tools/codex-contact/README.md">versioned client instructions</a> and repository setup prerequisites. The examples below reproduce the documented local command shape. They do not provision a server or establish a hosted connection.</p></section>
<section id="connection"><h2>1. Choose the account and connection</h2><p><a href="/register">Create an account</a> or <a href="/login">sign in</a>, then identify the workspace that should own your forms. An owner or admin can issue an expiring, revocable service token through the dashboard.</p><p>The draft connection needs <code>forms:read</code> and <code>forms:write</code>. It does not need <code>submissions:read</code>. Keep the credential in a user-only local secret store; load <code>GOFORMX_SERVICE_TOKEN</code> only for the client process. Never paste a management token into site code or a repository.</p><p>Set <code>$cli</code> to the absolute path of <code>tools/codex-contact/goformx_contact.py</code>, and <code>$org</code> to the selected organization ID. These are local PowerShell examples with placeholder identifiers:</p><pre tabindex="0" aria-label="Local site discovery commands"><code>python $cli --api-origin http://127.0.0.1:8080 --organization-id $org ensure-site --name 'Site A' --site-origin https://site-a.example
python $cli --api-origin http://127.0.0.1:8080 --organization-id $org discover --site-id $site</code></pre><p>Use the returned site ID for <code>$site</code>. Your browser origin must match the stored origin exactly. An organization ID is not a site ID.</p></section>
<section id="draft"><h2>2. Prepare and read back a draft</h2><p>Create <code>contact-form.json</code> with a name, title, the returned <code>siteId</code>, <code>allowedOrigins</code> and a Draft 2020-12 schema. The <a href="/docs#schema">schema guide</a> explains a minimal contact form.</p><pre tabindex="0" aria-label="Draft creation command"><code>python $cli --api-origin http://127.0.0.1:8080 --organization-id $org create-draft --intent site-a-contact-v1 --spec .\contact-form.json</code></pre><p>Keep the same intent and unchanged spec when retrying an uncertain response. The client persists an operation key before the request and reads back the accepted draft. Do not replace its private intent state to force a retry. Set <code>$form</code> to the exact returned form ID.</p></section>
<section id="integration"><h2>3. Generate browser-safe integration code</h2><pre tabindex="0" aria-label="Integration generation command"><code>python $cli --api-origin http://127.0.0.1:8080 --organization-id $org generate --form-id $form --output .\src\goformx-contact.js</code></pre><p>Connect the generated module to your site's actual fields and submit handler. It contains a public form key, allowed origin and schema version, never a management credential. Supply a stable 16–128 character idempotency key for each logical submission and reuse it if the outcome is uncertain.</p><p>Review the code locally. Generating a module does not prove a live form works. The generated module refuses to submit from another origin.</p></section>
<section id="publish"><h2>4. Review and explicitly publish</h2><p>Check the fields, limits, site, allowed origin and exact version. Publication requires a separate <code>forms:publish</code> grant and your explicit approval of that form and version. Draft creation never publishes automatically.</p><pre tabindex="0" aria-label="Explicit publication command"><code># Only after approval of this exact form and version 1
python $cli --api-origin http://127.0.0.1:8080 --organization-id $org publish --form-id $form --version 1 --confirm</code></pre><p>The public submission endpoint accepts published schemas only. There is no supported draft-only server submission preview in this client slice.</p></section>
<section id="receipt"><h2>5. Test synthetically, then check the inbox</h2><p>Use synthetic data in your disposable local environment. Do not test against someone else's live form.</p><pre tabindex="0" aria-label="Synthetic local submission command"><code>python $cli --api-origin http://127.0.0.1:8080 --organization-id $org test-submission --form-id $form --intent site-a-test-v1 --synthetic-data .\synthetic-data.json</code></pre><p>Retry with the identical intent and payload to verify deduplication. The client checks CORS and accepted schema version. An owner or admin should separately inspect the exact accepted record in <strong>All submissions</strong>, using the intended site/form filter.</p><p>Revoke setup grants when they are no longer needed. Inbox receipt does not prove email notification or signed webhook delivery. Email notifications remain unverified.</p><a class="text-link" href="/docs#troubleshooting">Troubleshoot a failed step <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></section>
</div></div>
